@startuml User Workflow
!theme plain
skinparam actorStyle awesome

title TestCaptive - User Workflow (Current vs Enterprise)

|#LightBlue|QA Engineer|
start

:Open Web Application;

|#LightGreen|Chrome Extension|
:Click Record Button;
:Monitor User Actions;

|#LightBlue|QA Engineer|
:Perform Test Scenario;
note right
  - Navigate pages
  - Fill forms
  - Click buttons
  - **Right-click → Add Assertions**
  - Verify workflows
end note

|#LightGreen|Chrome Extension|
:Capture Events in Real-Time;
:Capture Assertions (7 types);
:Apply Smart Deduplication;
:Extract Element Selectors;
:Save Session to JSON;

|#LightBlue|QA Engineer|
:Stop Recording;
:Open VS Code;

|#Yellow|VS Code Extension|
:Import Session File;
:Display Captured Events;
:Display Assertions with ✅ icon;

|#LightBlue|QA Engineer|
:Review Event List;
:Review Assertions;
:Select Playwright Framework;

|#Yellow|VS Code Extension|
:Generate Test Code;
:Apply Template Processing;
:Generate Assertion Code;
:Optimize Selectors;

|#LightBlue|QA Engineer|
:Review Generated Code;

if (Code Quality OK?) then (yes)
  :Export Test File;
  :Export Test Data JSON;
  
  |#LightGreen|Ready for CI/CD|
  note right
    **✅ Assertions Included**
    - Text validations
    - Visibility checks
    - State validations
    - URL verifications
    - **No manual work needed!**
  end note
  
  :Add to test suite;
  :Commit to version control;
  :Configure in CI/CD;
  
else (no)
  |#Yellow|VS Code Extension|
  :Re-record specific steps;
endif

|#LightBlue|QA Engineer|
stop

floating note right
  **Enterprise Enhancements**
  - ✅ Smart assertion capture (DONE)
  - AI assertion suggestions
  - Auto-commit to Git
  - Direct CI/CD integration
  - Team review workflow
  - Test suite organization
  - Maintenance alerts
end note

@enduml
